// @run
// @log 1
// @log 4
// @log 99
// @log 12345
// @log 262140
// THE HEADLINE. Before `memory.grow` was reachable, one page — 65536 bytes — was
// the entire budget a VL program could ever address, and a store at 65536 was an
// unavoidable trap. webcraft's ask is "a few large Buffers at init"; two 32 KiB
// buffers already did not fit.
//
// After growing to four pages the program addresses [0, 262144), and the last
// legal i32 address is 262140. Both addresses written here — 65536 and 262140 —
// TRAP on a one-page memory, so this case cannot pass without the growth having
// actually happened.
//
// (`__memory_grow__` returns the previous page count, so the first line is 1.)
print(__memory_grow__(3))
print(__memory_size__())
__store_i32__(65536, 99)
print(__load_i32__(65536))
__store_i32__(262140, 12345)
print(__load_i32__(262140))
print(__memory_size__() * 65536 - 4)
